{
  "openrpc": "1.2.6",
  "info": {
    "title": "Volt bridge",
    "version": "1",
    "description": "The wire a Volt bridge serves over a Windows NAMED PIPE \u2014 \u0060volt.bridge.\u003Cvendor\u003E.\u003Cpid\u003E\u0060, one per live IDE; a client discovers the pipes by prefix. ONE REQUEST PER CONNECTION: the client writes one request and reads the answer; the bridge closes the connection after the terminal frame. Concurrent requests use separate connections.\n\nENCODING: UTF-8 without a BOM. Every frame is one JSON object on one line ending in \u0060\\n\u0060. A request may end in \u0060\\r\\n\u0060; a request that starts with a BOM is BAD_REQUEST; a request with no \u0060\\n\u0060 is answered once the client closes its side. A request is at most 64 MiB, the newline excluded.\n\nREQUEST: \u0060{ \u0022op\u0022: \u0022\u003Cmethod\u003E\u0022, \u0022protocol\u0022: 1, \u0022body\u0022: { ... } }\u0060 (schema \u0060Request\u0060). \u0060protocol\u0060 is a JSON integer; a request that states none or another is refused PROTOCOL_MISMATCH before its body is read. \u0060body\u0060 absent is \u0060{}\u0060; a \u0060null\u0060 body, a member the method does not have, or an unknown envelope member is BAD_REQUEST.\n\nANSWER: zero or more \u0060{\u0022progress\u0022: ProgressFrame}\u0060, then exactly one \u0060{\u0022result\u0022: \u003Cthe method\u0027s result\u003E}\u0060 or \u0060{\u0022error\u0022: {\u0022code\u0022, \u0022message\u0022, \u0022data\u0022?}}\u0060 (schema \u0060ErrorFrame\u0060). A value a bridge does not list in its \u0060health\u0060 catalog (\u0060ops\u0060, \u0060languages\u0060, \u0060kinds\u0060) is one it never sends.\n\nGENERATED from the C# contract types and the hosts\u0027 declarations by \u0060DocDataTests\u0060; edit those, not this file."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "name": "named-pipe",
      "url": "npipe://./pipe/volt.bridge.{vendor}.{pid}",
      "summary": "One pipe per live IDE. Discover by PREFIX \u2014 the pid suffix changes when the IDE restarts.",
      "variables": {
        "vendor": {
          "default": "codesys",
          "enum": [
            "codesys",
            "twincat"
          ]
        },
        "pid": {
          "default": "0",
          "description": "The IDE process id the bridge is attached to."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "methods": [
    {
      "name": "health",
      "summary": "Liveness, the bridge\u0027s catalog and the connectable projects, from the bridge\u0027s cached snapshot \u2014 never on the IDE thread, so it answers while a push or build runs. While paused every row reads idle.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "Answers from the bridge\u0027s cached snapshot, never on the IDE thread: it answers while a push or build runs, never reports PLC_DISCONNECTED, and is not gated by \u0060disconnect\u0060 \u2014 while paused every row is \u0060idle\u0060.",
        "Answers on an IDE the bridge cannot serve: \u0060unsupported\u0060 carries the sentence every other op answers IDE_UNSUPPORTED with, and every row is idle. An IDE is refused for what it lacks, never for its version number.",
        "States the bridge identity at top level, rows or not: \u0060productName\u0060, \u0060productVersion\u0060, \u0060productVendor\u0060, \u0060ideVersion\u0060 (the platform under the product) and \u0060bridgeVersion\u0060 (the stamped release, or \u0060(dev) \u003Ccommit\u003E\u0060). Each is absent when its source does not answer, never filled from another.",
        "States the bridge\u0027s catalog, from its own declarations: \u0060ops\u0060 (every op it answers), \u0060languages\u0060 (every language it writes as \u0060IMPLEMENTATION \u003CLANG\u003E\u0060) and \u0060kinds\u0060 (every item kind, by extension, and whether a push writes it). A value the bridge does not list there is one it never sends.",
        "A row\u0027s \u0060dirty\u0060 is absent when the IDE did not answer whether the project is saved: unknown, never clean."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HealthResponse"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "connect",
      "summary": "Bind a project and resume service. An absent or empty \u0060project\u0060 means \u0022serve whatever you have\u0022. Refuses with PLC_DISCONNECTED unless the bridge ends up serving the named project.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConnectRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED when the bridge does not end up serving the named project: it attached nothing, or something other than the project named. \u0060project\u0060 is compared like a path, ignoring case.",
        "A refused connect still leaves the bridge resumed: a \u0060disconnect\u0060 racing a connect wins."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EmptyResult"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "disconnect",
      "summary": "Pause the bridge: refuse sync until the next connect, tear nothing down. Answers even while a push is running, and that push runs to completion.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "Sets a flag and answers, without the IDE thread: it answers while a push runs, and that push runs to completion. The flag stops the next op, never the current one."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EmptyResult"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "refs",
      "summary": "The version map without any content: the path \u2192 version map and \u0060projectVersion\u0060. This is what a client compares against to decide what to fetch.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RefsRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
        "WRONG_PROJECT",
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED as an error frame (TwinCAT): the Solution Explorer cannot vouch for the PLC project itself, so the walk stops before anything is read. Fix what stops the IDE enumerating it.",
        "An item whose body will not materialize is no error: it is in \u0060unreadable\u0060 with its code, and keeps a stable version so a pull does not read it as deleted.",
        "A read is retried once through a transient IDE failure; \u0060health\u0060 reports the session degraded meanwhile.",
        "Progress frames start with the walk: one per application as the walk finishes it, \u0060phase: \u0022walking\u0022\u0060, \u0060done\u0060 applications of \u0060total\u0060 (a TwinCAT PLC project is an application; CODESYS states no \u0060total\u0060). The item frames follow: the first with its phase and \u0060done\u0060 0 of \u0060total\u0060 items, then one every 25 items and one at the last.",
        "A \u0060refs\u0060 that arrives while one with the same body runs joins it: it receives that one\u0027s progress frames from then on and the same terminal frame. Nothing is kept once it answers: the next \u0060refs\u0060 walks again."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RefsResponse"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "fetch",
      "summary": "Item CONTENT. \u0060knownItems\u0060 narrows the answer to what changed; \u0060onlyItems\u0060 restricts it to a named subset. Naming a \u0060.library\u0060 returns its manifest and every signature of that library, in the folder and with the bytes a full fetch writes; \u0060libraryManifestOnly\u0060 answers the manifest alone. Graphical bodies arrive as network text.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FetchRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
        "WRONG_PROJECT",
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED as an error frame (TwinCAT): the Solution Explorer cannot vouch for the PLC project itself, so the walk stops before anything is read. Fix what stops the IDE enumerating it.",
        "BAD_REQUEST for a fetch with neither \u0060knownItems\u0060 nor \u0060onlyItems\u0060 nor \u0060init: true\u0060.",
        "A known path under a folder the walk could not read is never in \u0060removed\u0060; one absent from a folder it did read is.",
        "Items that would not materialize are in \u0060unreadable\u0060, not raised.",
        "Progress frames start with the walk: one per application as the walk finishes it, \u0060phase: \u0022walking\u0022\u0060, \u0060done\u0060 applications of \u0060total\u0060 (a TwinCAT PLC project is an application; CODESYS states no \u0060total\u0060). The item frames follow: the first with its phase and \u0060done\u0060 0 of \u0060total\u0060 items, then one every 25 items and one at the last."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FetchResponse"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "push",
      "summary": "Apply ops to the IDE. Every text-decidable refusal runs in a pre-flight before the first write. \u0060expectedProjectVersion\u0060 is the lease; per-item \u0060ifVersion\u0060 is the optimistic guard.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PushRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
        "WRONG_PROJECT",
        "STALE_PROJECT_VERSION",
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED",
        "IDE_BUSY"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED as an error frame (TwinCAT): the Solution Explorer cannot vouch for the PLC project itself, so the walk stops before anything is read. Fix what stops the IDE enumerating it.",
        "IDE_BUSY when another push or build holds the IDE: refused at once, before the IDE is touched, so nothing is applied or compiled. Reads and \u0060health\u0060 are never refused with it. Wait for the running op, then try once.",
        "BAD_REQUEST when \u0060expectedPlatform\u0060 or \u0060expectedProjectName\u0060 is absent or empty, naming each missing member, before anything is walked: a write names the project it writes. The reads keep both optional.",
        "STALE_PROJECT_VERSION when \u0060expectedProjectVersion\u0060 is not the project\u0027s version: nothing is applied, and \u0060error.data.currentProjectVersion\u0060 is the version the IDE holds.",
        "Writes into the open project and saves nothing: the engineer saves.",
        "A refused op is no error frame: it is a conflict in the result, named by the op\u0027s \u0060name\u0060, with its code. Every op \u0060conflicts\u0060 does not name landed in full.",
        "A refusal decidable before the first write lands nothing: each refused op answers its code, every other op NOT_ATTEMPTED.",
        "A refusal during the apply lands the ops before it and stops: the refused op answers its code, every later op NOT_ATTEMPTED.",
        "\u0060newProjectVersion\u0060 is present exactly when something landed; \u0060newItems\u0060 and \u0060removed\u0060 are what the push changed, so \u0060baseline \u2212 removed \u002B newItems\u0060 is the IDE after it.",
        "What of a refused op the IDE kept is stated on its conflict: \u0060partiallyApplied\u0060, \u0060renamedTo\u0060, \u0060remains\u0060 \u2014 each absent when it does not apply."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PushResponse"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "build",
      "summary": "Compile the bound project and return the IDE\u0027s own diagnostics.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BuildRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
        "WRONG_PROJECT",
        "IDE_BUSY",
        "UNSUPPORTED"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "IDE_BUSY when another push or build holds the IDE: refused at once, before the IDE is touched, so nothing is applied or compiled. Reads and \u0060health\u0060 are never refused with it. Wait for the running op, then try once.",
        "BAD_REQUEST when \u0060expectedPlatform\u0060 or \u0060expectedProjectName\u0060 is absent or empty, naming each missing member, before anything is walked: a write names the project it writes. The reads keep both optional.",
        "UNSUPPORTED for a project that holds no application (a CODESYS library project): there is nothing to build.",
        "BAD_REQUEST for an \u0060applications\u0060 root the project does not hold, or an empty list, before anything is built. Named roots build those applications alone and report only their diagnostics; absent, every application is built.",
        "A project that does not compile is \u0060success: false\u0060 with its diagnostics, never an error frame; a compile that throws answers \u0060success: false\u0060 with the reason as an error diagnostic.",
        "\u0060success\u0060 is each vendor\u0027s own signal: CODESYS has it from its diagnostics, TwinCAT from the IDE\u0027s count of failed projects. A failed build always carries an error diagnostic: when the IDE wrote none Volt could read, one says so, with no position.",
        "\u0060severity\u0060 is absent when the vendor\u0027s value is not in its host\u0027s declared table. \u0060line\u0060 and \u0060column\u0060 are 1-based lines and columns of the item\u0027s fetched \u0060sourceText\u0060, absent when the vendor stated none or the bridge cannot place one there: CODESYS states no position, TwinCAT a line and no column.",
        "Compiles what the IDE holds in memory; Volt calls no save. On TwinCAT a build saves changed documents, as XAE\u0027s own Build does."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BuildResponse"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "grep",
      "summary": "Search the text \u0060fetch\u0060 ships for each item, line by line, and answer the matching LINES \u2014 path, 1-based line, the line as fetched \u2014 with each matched item\u0027s \u0060refs\u0060 version, never whole sources. A regular expression or \u0060literal\u0060 text, ignoring case unless \u0060caseSensitive\u0060; \u0060paths\u0060 globs limit what is searched. What could not be searched is in \u0060notSearched\u0060.",
      "paramStructure": "by-name",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "required": false,
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GrepRequest"
          }
        }
      ],
      "x-errorCodes": [
        "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
        "BAD_REQUEST",
        "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
        "INTERNAL_ERROR",
        "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
        "WRONG_PROJECT",
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED"
      ],
      "x-outcomes": [
        "ITEM_UNVERIFIED as an error frame (TwinCAT): the Solution Explorer cannot vouch for the PLC project itself, so the walk stops before anything is read. Fix what stops the IDE enumerating it.",
        "BAD_REQUEST, before the walk, for an empty \u0060pattern\u0060, a regular expression that does not compile (the parse error named) or a \u0060limit\u0060 outside 1\u20131000; and, with no partial answer, for a pattern that takes longer than 100 ms on one line.",
        "What it searches is what \u0060fetch\u0060 ships as text, from the same walk: a matched line is the fetched line at that number. An \u0060unreadable\u0060 item, and a body that reads \u0060IMPLEMENTATION \u003CLANG\u003E UNSUPPORTED\u0060, are in \u0060notSearched\u0060 with a code; libraries are not searched and not listed.",
        "The answer is bounded: at most \u0060limit\u0060 matches, counted up to 10000 in \u0060totalMatches\u0060; \u0060truncated\u0060 when more were found than answered. A line longer than 500 UTF-16 code units is cut, ends in \u0060\u2026\u0060 and carries \u0060cut: true\u0060."
      ],
      "result": {
        "name": "result",
        "schema": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GrepResponse"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "BridgeDiagnostic": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "member": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "severity": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "error",
              "warning",
              "info"
            ]
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "1-based line of the item\u0027s FETCHED \u0060sourceText\u0060 (the coordinates of \u0060grep\u0060 and of a network-text conflict\u0027s \u0060line\u0060), never the vendor\u0027s own count. Absent when the vendor stated none or the bridge cannot place it in that text with certainty (a property accessor\u0027s line, a network or hidden body)."
          },
          "column": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "1-based column on \u0060line\u0060, as the vendor stated it; absent when it stated none, and always without \u0060line\u0060."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "message"
        ]
      },
      "BridgeErrorCode": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "A Volt code: why an op was refused (error frame), why an op of a push did not land (conflict), or why an object was not read (unreadable). The channels each arrives on are in the code table.",
        "enum": [
          "PROTOCOL_MISMATCH",
          "STALE_PROJECT_VERSION",
          "PLC_DISCONNECTED",
          "WRONG_PROJECT",
          "IDE_LOST_ITEM",
          "BAD_REQUEST",
          "UNSUPPORTED",
          "DUPLICATE_CHILD",
          "INVALID_ST",
          "UNREADABLE",
          "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
          "IDE_BUSY",
          "INTERNAL_ERROR",
          "ITEM_UNVERIFIED"
        ]
      },
      "BuildRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "applications": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "expectedPlatform": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "codesys",
              "twincat"
            ]
          },
          "expectedProjectName": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "expectedPlatform",
          "expectedProjectName"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "BuildResponse": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "success": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "durationMs": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "diagnostics": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BridgeDiagnostic"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "success",
          "durationMs",
          "diagnostics"
        ]
      },
      "ConflictCode": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The code of a push conflict: the gate\u0027s, a bridge refusal of the op, NOT_ATTEMPTED, or a network-text refusal of the body (every NETWORK_ code, and only one, comes with the conflict\u0027s \u0060line\u0060).",
        "enum": [
          "STALE_ITEM_VERSION",
          "ITEM_EXISTS",
          "ITEM_MISSING",
          "ITEM_UNVERIFIED",
          "IDE_LOST_ITEM",
          "UNSUPPORTED",
          "DUPLICATE_CHILD",
          "BAD_REQUEST",
          "INVALID_ST",
          "UNREADABLE",
          "IDE_UNSUPPORTED",
          "INTERNAL_ERROR",
          "NOT_ATTEMPTED",
          "NETWORK_PARSE",
          "NETWORK_NOT_CLOSED",
          "NETWORK_DUPLICATE_NAME",
          "NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION",
          "NETWORK_UNKNOWN_OPERATOR",
          "NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED"
        ]
      },
      "ConnectRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "DeleteItemOp": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "ifVersion": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "op": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "deleteItem"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "EmptyResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      },
      "ErrorFrame": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The terminal frame of a refused op. \u0060data\u0060 is present for the codes that carry facts: PROTOCOL_MISMATCH (\u0060ProtocolMismatchData\u0060) and STALE_PROJECT_VERSION (\u0060StaleProjectVersionData\u0060).",
        "properties": {
          "error": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "code": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BridgeErrorCode"
              },
              "message": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "data": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProtocolMismatchData"
                  },
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StaleProjectVersionData"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "code",
              "message"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "error"
        ]
      },
      "FetchRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "knownItems": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "knownApplications": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "onlyItems": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "libraryManifestOnly": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "init": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "expectedPlatform": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "codesys",
              "twincat"
            ]
          },
          "expectedProjectName": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "FetchResponse": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "changed": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FetchedItem"
            }
          },
          "librariesRefreshed": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "projectVersion": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "applications": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "unreadable": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UnreadableItem"
            }
          },
          "unreadableNodes": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UnreadableNode"
            }
          },
          "removed": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "unwalkedFolders": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "platform": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "codesys",
              "twincat"
            ]
          },
          "projectName": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "changed",
          "librariesRefreshed",
          "projectVersion",
          "items",
          "applications",
          "unreadable",
          "unreadableNodes",
          "removed",
          "unwalkedFolders"
        ]
      },
      "FetchedItem": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "sourceText": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "version": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "unsupported": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UnsupportedBody"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "sourceText",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "GrepMatch": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "line": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "cut": {
